Having just acquired the newer version of Slash'Em, and having hunted
through the various spoilers I could find for explanations of a number of
the newer features (I'm still playing version 0.0.3e3, so 0.0.7 is quite a
dramatic change), I can't find anything explaining the costs, benefits,
and strategies of having a steed, as opposed to a generic pet. I've tried
it a bit, and am still puzzled about it. After all, if one wants to pick
things up from a horse, one almost always has to dismount (a fishing pole
is tricky to use and doesn't grab everything), at least early on in the
process - and constant mounting/dismounting apparently untames the steed.
It's also a lot of trouble keeping a horse fed (especially if you're a
monk!), etc. - but none of the spoilers explain what really nifty
long-term benefits accrue. I can only *suspect* a few benefits (haven't
yet seen them, but I suppose they are possible): jumping/flying over
obstacles, galloping, and having a little more direct defense if I'm
incapacitated momentarily but the steed is not. Not being a source-diver,
I can't tell if you get hungry slower when riding, but that isn't
illogical.

Is there a spoiler I've missed, or is this something that someone could
write up? It seems like an obvious omission, to me.

